  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Discovery and focused evidence • no trading authority",
      "items": [
        "Six code-owned search lanes: broad, SEC, issuer IR, reporting, undercovered wire and rotating sector. A one-turn tool-free selector admits at most five source-bound company/event pairs; policy skips never admit a sixth lead. Discovery does not require a two-source bundle.",
        "Focused search, safety validation and fair allocation admit up to five URLs per candidate / 25 unique URLs; at most three singleton extraction supervisors run concurrently under one original deadline. Actual extraction envelopes, not search/model prose, establish page content; accepted focused pages can be reused.",
        "Ordinary fetch/cache, SEC dates and publication recovery precede ranking. At least two distinct accepted publisher domains are required. Evidence score uses provenance, independent/primary corroboration, completeness and freshness; scout order breaks ties."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Admission gate • activation-gated opportunity policy and research memory",
      "items": [
        "No activation record keeps the legacy floor: exact-dossier review protection, no event allowance. Activated v1/v2 resolves trusted SEC issuer/event identity and skips spent generations, held symbols and same-symbol pending entries; unknown or conflicting identity fails closed. v2 binds candidates to one approved prospective baseline.",
        "Activated v3 retires event admission: exact-document research memory keyed by verified issuer, representation, content digest and rules. Completed work is reusable for under 24 hours, failed resources cool down 20 minutes, and a memory hit reuses a still-fresh unreviewed dossier or skips a duplicate bundle. Cache damage runs uncached; it never relaxes history or execution checks.",
        "Outside v3 memory mode, acquisition-hinted leads are retained privately as research-only records and never become candidates. SEC identity capture uses bounded exact-URL fetches inside the remaining evidence deadline; no model, broker or new allowance. Activation needs an explicit approved-digest admin apply and was not inspected."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Rescue, sequential alternatives and distinct failure paths",
      "items": [
        "Thin-bundle rescue preserves accepted evidence and resumes bounded operation turns across up to three candidates: retained alternatives, SEC primary lookup, then missing independent/wire lane searches. Proven spent/held facts can prune rescue; unknown thin bundles still receive it. Rescue does not reset recovery or evidence budgets.",
        "Up to five distinct evidence-eligible symbols receive sequential tool-free synthesis plus the same deterministic intake. Explicit none / candidate-local rejection continues; first intake pass returns immediately. Infrastructure, parse, containment, market-data ambiguity and persistence failures abort rather than trying another candidate.",
        "When every remaining lead is policy-skipped or retained as research-only, Radar reports no_new_eligible_opportunity (exit 0). A mixed run whose last attempt ends in an ordinary none keeps the no_fresh_setup class."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Shared budgets, exit-aware earnings and actual data adapters",
      "items": [
        "Synthesis: 270 cumulative seconds across all candidates, no per-candidate cap. Enrichment: separate 90 cumulative seconds. Enrichment pauses synthesis charging but still consumes the 960-second absolute active deadline; outer research wrapper is 990 seconds. Minimum viable launch/reserve checks still apply.",
        "Prompt anchors actual UTC and New York as-of times and requires a future timezone-aware UTC ISO exit with 1–30 entry-inclusive holding sessions. No date repair. Intake checks exit-aware earnings through planned exit plus weekday blackout; the unchanged broker actual-session earnings gate remains authoritative.",
        "Enrichment resolves trusted earnings and synchronized completed stock/SPY prices via Massive REST (credential read from Massive MCP configuration). Alpaca MCP supplies account/order/calendar and IEX quote truth. FRED is not integrated. Radar CLI runs also write a private best-effort enrichment trace (max 124 rows per attempt); it changes no budget, routing or gate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Producer / consumer cadence • New York time",
      "items": [
        "Premarket 09:00 ET; radar 10:00–15:40 at :00/:20/:40. Autotrader UTC grid: 18,38,58 13-20 * * 1-5; NY slot AND weekday 09:30–16:00 fence accept 09:38/09:58, then 10:18–15:58 at :18/:38/:58. 09:18 and off-window fires do not execute; broker regular-session validation remains authoritative.",
        "Radar-to-consumer spacing is 18 minutes; 990-second wrapper leaves nominal 90 seconds, not guaranteed non-overlap. Reconciliation uses a separate :02/:12/:22/:32/:42/:52 grid and the shared nonblocking entry lock. Code-defined schedules are not installed-job readback.",
        "A cron-shaped pre-open URL-admission check wrapper is validation-only (config/DNS reads; no fetch, model, broker or ledger write): silent on pass, one SYSTEM_FAILURE line and exit 3 on failure. No committed schedule time; it does not prove research health."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Execution controls • checked-in configuration",
      "items": [
        "Pinned configuration: enabled=true, paper; discovery_v2, focused retrieval and gap retrieval enabled. exact_owned_zero_fill_v1 permits three qualified pending parents. Daily cap is three submissions, including unknown submissions by original New York submission date.",
        "Unchanged observed limits: $10,000 managed exposure; $500 per position; planned risk <=$40; IEX spread <=600 bps; whole shares; no margin. These are checked-in settings, not new policy authorization.",
        "Gross cash reserves exact pending notional once; available-net buying power is a separate cap and is not reduced twice. Pending notional also reserves exposure headroom. Unknown funding, manual/unlinked orders, partial fills and same-symbol pending entries block."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Independent decision, not model-selected order fields",
      "items": [
        "Under an activated policy, any positive broker position blocks a new BUY (no add-on) before sizing and paid review; bounded broker observations must be under 120 seconds old and read within 120 seconds. The exact approved attempt is re-proven and rechecked under the entry lock before intent.",
        "Python fixes ask, completed-bar levels, shares and entry metadata before hashing. Both independent tool-free reviewers receive that immutable proposal; only exact APPROVE/HOLD outputs are persisted, anything else is recorded as reviewer-unavailable. Both must approve; lower score >=0.55; R/R >=1.6.",
        "New short 1–5-session intents expire at placement-session regular close; swing 6–30 at the next actual session close. Authoritative New York calendar handles early closes, DST and holidays. Entry deadline is not the investment holding deadline."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Source pin, not operational or deployment evidence",
      "items": [
        "Frozen committed source: 6958777. This documentation refresh does not deploy, activate policies or schedules, inspect accounts, call models or execute broker actions. Artifact checks establish diagram integrity, not runtime acceptance or release approval.",
        "Expiry is OBSERVATION ONLY: SAFE_PARENT_CANCEL_VERIFIED=False. Legacy intents without metadata are never retrofitted. Passing a deadline never frees a slot, cash/exposure reservation or daily quota; exact confirmed lifecycle reconciliation is required.",
        "Reconciliation journals a saved pending entry only on an exact broker full fill (journal before lifecycle row; idempotent fill key). A saved partial readback may advance only to that exact full fill; partial accounting stays unsupported. verify_only reports managed_repair_required instead of writing.",
        "Stable outer Linux subreaper owns inner supervisor, wrapper and detached orphans. Caller pidfd and inherited entry-lock descriptions preserve authority until owned descendants are reaped. External custodian SIGKILL/OOM, container death and uninterruptible tasks remain outside the guarantee; no sandbox or broker rollback."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Portfolio watchdog • independent monitoring, never execution",
      "items": [
        "Mechanical: UTC 5 14-21 * * 1-5, only :05 inside a verified session; protection, quantity, exit horizon and exposure. Hard bound: 120 seconds.",
        "Daily: UTC 15,45 17-22 * * 1-5, only close+15 / close+45. Adds managed-strategy versus account accounting, benchmark coverage and versioned-thesis monitoring. Hard bound: 900 seconds.",
        "Both read broker and operational ledgers and write only monitoring outputs. Research memory is excluded from operational authority, so an absent cache cannot disable monitoring; order coalescing tolerates only sub-microsecond timestamp rounding. No order placement, cancellation, liquidation, journal repair or kill-switch changes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Coverage gaps stay visible • no invented safety or performance",
      "items": [
        "Missing lineage, legacy baselines, incomplete financial evidence, unknown exact earnings times and benchmark gaps remain typed coverage limitations. SEC metadata is not extracted financial content.",
        "A fully observed cancelled stop or expired holding horizon still forbids all-clear. Classification is a stateless, tool-free provider request; source workers do not receive broker credentials.",
        "Watchdog state is shared under private/watchdog/: observations, condition state, source cutoffs, reports and alert outbox. Public output is field/value allowlisted, never raw source or model prose."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Reporting retry and delivery • completion is not acknowledgment",
      "items": [
        "The later daily slot retries report installation, pending-outbox delivery and completion marker only after an observation is already committed; it does not repeat thesis retrieval or claim fresh all-clear.",
        "Mechanical runs without exceptions are silent; daily successful runs emit a report/coverage summary. Out-of-slot launches are silent no-ops, not completed observations.",
        "Hermes cron relays sanitized stdout, not a provider receipt. Schema 1 retains legacy receiptless replay. Explicitly activated schema 2 separately records suppression/prepared/emitted/failed; urgent conditions remind after 24h and one daily summary follows installation. Emitted is not delivered. Activation was not inspected."
      ]
    }
  ]
}